  "closureReview": {
    "decision": "PENDING"
  },
  "scopeDecisions": [
    {
      "id": "R1",
      "decision": "Closure is defined by these behavioral acceptance conditions, observed with end-user credentials (no credential, or an ID token issued by the same project's Auth) through Firestore REST v1 and gRPC google.firestore.v1 against the disposable Identity Platform sandbox, whose Firestore and Rules this lane owns. Administrator credentials bypass Rules and are used only to prepare and clean up.",
      "decidedBy": "owner (t-k)",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-24"
    },
    {
      "id": "R2",
      "decision": "gRPC Listen, WebChannel and client SDK paths belong to FS-LISTEN-SDK; Auth state changes observed by listeners and SDKs (sign-out, token refresh while listening, revocation during a listen) belong to AUTH-FS-CROSS.",
      "decidedBy": "owner (t-k)",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-24",
      "movedTo": "FS-LISTEN-SDK"
    },
    {
      "id": "R3",
      "decision": "Token issuance, refresh and verification by Identity Toolkit and Secure Token belong to AUTH-CREDENTIAL; this parent observes only what Firestore and Rules do with the token they receive (AUTH-CREDENTIAL scope decision C3).",
      "decidedBy": "owner (t-k)",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-24",
      "movedTo": "AUTH-CREDENTIAL"
    },
    {
      "id": "R4",
      "decision": "The Firebase Rules API resources (projects.rulesets, projects.releases, compile issue details, release readback) are a known difference outside this parent: fireemu does not implement them. This parent compares the effect of a publication: decisions after a release switch, compile acceptance or refusal, and refusal of every request without a release.",
      "decidedBy": "owner (t-k)",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-24"
    },
    {
      "id": "R5",
      "decision": "Production propagates a release switch over tens of seconds, during which different frontends answer with the old and the new ruleset. fireemu switches atomically. The delay is an approved divergence that fireemu does not reproduce; conditions compare decisions after propagation.",
      "decidedBy": "owner (t-k)",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-24"
    },
    {
      "id": "R6",
      "decision": "A Rules denial answers with production's status and text (PERMISSION_DENIED, \"Missing or insufficient permissions.\") in both profiles. The reason stays available in fireemu's request traces and log. The emulator-profile change is listed in CHANGELOG and contract.json fireemuOnly.",
      "decidedBy": "owner (t-k)",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-24"
    },
    {
      "id": "R7",
      "decision": "Tenant principals are observed here: the sandbox enables multi-tenancy and creates one tenant for the run, deleted afterwards.",
      "decidedBy": "owner (t-k)",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-24"
    },
    {
      "id": "R8",
      "decision": "Named databases are observed on a small scale: two named databases per recording, one with its own release and one without, created and deleted by the recording.",
      "decidedBy": "owner (t-k)",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-24",
      "revisedOn": "2026-09-25"
    },
    {
      "id": "R9",
      "decision": "The strict profile is the comparison profile. The emulator profile may add no refusal: it keeps accepting unsigned emulator tokens and allows every request while no ruleset is loaded, as the official emulator does. Its differences from production are listed per condition, not compared.",
      "decidedBy": "owner (t-k), handoff 2026-09-24",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-24"
    },
    {
      "id": "R10",
      "decision": "Cloud Storage Security Rules and the Storage-to-Firestore functions are outside the Firebase Auth and Firestore production-compatibility program.",
      "decidedBy": "owner (t-k), handoff 2026-09-24",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-24"
    }
  ],
